# Next.js Skills — Default Rules When Writing Code

These rules are derived from [claude-nextjs-skills](https://github.com/wsimmonds/claude-nextjs-skills) and apply by default when writing or editing Next.js pages and components in this project.

---

## TypeScript: NEVER Use `any`

- This codebase uses strict TypeScript. Using `any` can cause build failures.
- Use proper types: `React.FormEvent<HTMLFormElement>`, `params: Promise<{ id: string }>`, `searchParams: Promise<{ q?: string }>`, etc.

---

## App Router Basics

- **Routes**: File-based under `src/app/`. `page.tsx` = route UI, `layout.tsx` = segment wrapper, `loading.tsx` / `error.tsx` for loading/error.
- **Root layout**: Must include `<html>` and `<body>`. No `next/head`; use `export const metadata` or `generateMetadata`.
- **Navigation**: Use `<Link href="...">` from `next/link` for links. Use `redirect()` from `next/navigation` for server-side redirects. Do **not** add `'use client'` just for links.
- **Server vs Client**: Default is Server Component. Add `'use client'` only when you need hooks, event handlers, or browser APIs.

---

## Server vs Client Components

- **Server (default)**: Can `await` in the component, use `cookies()`, `headers()`, fetch data directly. No `'use client'`.
- **Client**: Needs `'use client'` at top of file. Use for `useState`, `useEffect`, `onClick`, `window`, etc.
- **Critical**: Do **not** use `cookies()` or `headers()` in a Client Component. Read them in a Server Component and pass data as props (or call a server action from client to set cookies).
- **useSearchParams**: Requires **both** `'use client'` **and** the component wrapped in `<Suspense>`. Always wrap any component that uses `useSearchParams()` in a parent `<Suspense>`.
- **Navigation in Server Components**: Use `<Link>` and `redirect()`. Do **not** use `useRouter()` in a Server Component; use `useRouter()` only in Client Components for programmatic navigation.

---

## Params and searchParams (Next.js 15+)

- **params**: In App Router pages/layouts, `params` is a **Promise**. Type as `params: Promise<{ id: string }>` and **await** it: `const { id } = await params`.
- **searchParams**: In `page.tsx`, `searchParams` can be a Promise in Next.js 15+. Prefer inline access when extracting: `const q = (await searchParams).q ?? ''`.
- **Client Components**: Cannot receive `params` directly. Use `useParams()` from `next/navigation`, or pass the id/slug as a prop from a Server Component.

---

## Dynamic Routes

- Use **simplest structure** unless the requirement explicitly specifies a path. Prefer `app/[id]/page.tsx` over `app/products/[id]/page.tsx` when the requirement is just "fetch by ID."
- Folder name must use brackets: `[id]`, `[slug]`, `[...slug]`, `[[...slug]]`.
- In `route.ts` (Route Handlers), `params` is also a Promise: `{ params }: { params: Promise<{ id: string }> }` and must be awaited.

---

## Anti-Patterns to Avoid

1. **Do not use `useEffect` for initial data fetching** — Use a Server Component and `await fetch()` (or data layer) in the component. Use React Query/SWR in Client Components only when you need client-side refetch/mutations.
2. **Do not use `useState` for server-fetched data** — Fetch in Server Component and pass as props.
3. **Do not use `useEffect` for browser detection** — Use direct check in component body with `typeof navigator !== 'undefined'` and conditional render, or use CSS/media where possible.
4. **Do not use `getServerSideProps` / `getStaticProps`** — Use async Server Components and `fetch(..., { next: { revalidate } })` or `cache()`.
5. **Do not use `next/head`** — Use `metadata` export or `generateMetadata`.
6. **Do not use serial `await` when independent** — Use `Promise.all([fetchA(), fetchB()])` or separate `<Suspense>` boundaries.
7. **Do not add `'use client'` to the root layout or to whole pages** — Add it only to the smallest component that needs client features.
8. **Do not import a Server Component into a Client Component** — Pass the Server Component as **children** from a parent Server Component so it stays server-rendered.
9. **Do not use `window.location.href` for in-app navigation** — Use `<Link>` or `useRouter().push()`.
10. **Do not create API routes just to fetch data for a single page** — Fetch (or access DB) directly in the Server Component unless you need a public API or webhook.

---

## Server Actions

- **Location**: Under `app/` (e.g. `app/actions.ts` or `app/dashboard/action.ts`). Use `'use server'` at top of file or inside the function.
- **Setting cookies**: Only server code can set cookies. For a button/click that sets a cookie, use a Client Component that calls a server action which uses `cookies()` from `next/headers` and `cookieStore.set(...)`.
- **Form actions**: When using `<form action={serverAction}>`, the action must return **void** (no return value). Validate and `throw new Error(...)` on failure, or use `useActionState` if you need to return success/error state to the UI.
- **Never mix** `'use server'` and `'use client'` in the same file. Server actions live in their own file; client components import and call them.

---

## Route Handlers (API Routes)

- Live in `app/api/.../route.ts`. Export `GET`, `POST`, etc. Return `Response` or `Response.json()`.
- For dynamic segments: `{ params }: { params: Promise<{ id: string }> }` and `const { id } = await params`.

---

## Error and Loading UI

- Use `error.tsx` (Client Component) for error boundaries and `loading.tsx` for loading UI. Use `not-found.tsx` and call `notFound()` when a resource is missing.

---

## Quick Checklist When Writing a Next.js Page

- [ ] Is it a Server Component by default? Only add `'use client'` if the component needs hooks or browser APIs.
- [ ] Using `params`? Type as `Promise<...>` and `await params` (Next.js 15+).
- [ ] Using `useSearchParams()`? Component has `'use client'` and is wrapped in `<Suspense>`.
- [ ] Navigation? Use `<Link>` in Server or Client; use `redirect()` in Server; use `useRouter()` only in Client.
- [ ] Data fetch? Prefer Server Component with direct fetch or data layer; avoid `useEffect` + fetch for initial load.
- [ ] Setting a cookie from UI? Client component calls a server action that uses `cookies()` and `cookieStore.set()`.
- [ ] No `any`; use proper event and prop types.

Source: [wsimmonds/claude-nextjs-skills](https://github.com/wsimmonds/claude-nextjs-skills) — applied as default rules for this dashboard.
